            "review_text": "Sol de Villa R\n2 contributions\n0\nMy very bad experience@ Thuy Ta Resto\nJan 2025 • Family\nWe entered this resto - Thuy Ta, at around 1:30pm to eat brunch. We asked one of the crew what is the closing time of the resto, and she told me that until 1am. So, I said to my daughter and niece that we shall stay here until midnight to witness the fireworks in celebration of the Lunar New Year. So, from brunch, to coffee time, to dinner, we ordered in this resto. At around 10pm, after dinner and coffee, we were approached by a male crew and told us that we need to transfer to another table because the table we are occupying has been reserved, so we were told to take the opposite table, so we werw ushered to the said table. About 15 minutes layee, the male crew approaahed us again, and told us that we need to get out of the resto because the table we are occupying again was intended for those who bought tickets or has reservation for the observant of the fireworks, unless we will buy a ticket worth 600 vnd for each of us. This was not explained to us by the female crew who ushered us earlier, I told the male crew. After spending almost 2 million vnd here, we are being asked to get out of the resto? Is this fair? I asked the crew to tell the manager about our case. About 10 minutes, the Manager came, hoping he will explain to us something, but to my dismay, he just told us that the female crew who ushered us earlier has no knowledge of the policy, and that we need to get out of the resto and vacate the table we are occupying! imagine his words,no explanation at all? where is the justice in here, Mr Manager, Mr resto owner? Is this how you treat your clients? My goodness, now I know, why your online rating review is generally poor! I still have other negative observations, will post it here one by one. I will give you negative 1 as a rating! Good you have a very good business location, if not, you will not prosper as a business!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 29, 2025",
