            "review_text": "Pham Cong Dung\nCat Ba, Vietnam1 contribution\n0\nPrime Location, Poor Quality: A Stark Contrast at the Restaurant\nNov 2024 • Family\nThis restaurant’s only redeeming quality is its location by the scenic Hoan Kiem Lake. Beyond that, it’s an endless string of disappointments. The food and drinks are prepared using questionable ingredients that fail to meet even the most basic hygiene and food safety standards, yet they’re priced sky-high.\n\nThe service? Absolutely abysmal. The staff are not only unprofessional but also show blatant disdain for customers. Even if you’ve ordered from their overpriced menu, bringing in your own bottled water or ice cream stick will result in an absurd surcharge.\n\nThe icing on the cake? Sewer rats casually scurrying around as if this were their domain, including in the kitchen – the very place that’s supposed to uphold cleanliness and safety. This restaurant isn’t just a disappointment; it’s a hazard to both your health and your wallet.\nRead more\nWritten November 23, 2024",
